# sphere-networking-live

At the start of every conversation, read `.cursor/skills/sphere-networking-live/SKILL.md` and follow it.

This is the default for this repository. Do not wait for the user to mention packets, MBC, or PacketLogViewer.

## Ground truth before hypotheses

If you ever need to analyze a behavior for the network protocol, first look into MBC decompile (`d:\Download\MBCdecompiler-main\`) and client recompile (`d:\Download\SferaClientRecompiled-main\`) before making hypotheses.

- Region `formats`, handler bytecode, and client `skipRegion`/`receiveRegion`/`readField`/`send` are authoritative.
- Do not invent adaptive width probes or dual-layout guessers when those sources already define the wire.
- If a capture disagrees, debug framing (region, start bit, module tag, origin). Do not override the catalog by guessing.

## Inferred names over MBC routines

Always use inferred semantic names (`mbc_commands.jsonl` `n`, recovered overrides) for PLV labels. Never use MBC routines (`CheckPing`, `ContMan`, `Manager`, `Owner`, …) as the primary event name; those are receive/send sites only.
